#: index.docbook:4816
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Command line options are provided to enable other programs to start up &kalarm; if it is not already running, in order to trigger or cancel scheduled alarms, or schedule new alarms. The reason for using command line options for this purpose is that if &kalarm; were started without any command line parameters and then sent D-Bus requests, it would start in its default graphical mode, which is clearly undesirable for an inter-program request."
msgid "Command line options are provided to enable other programs to start up &kalarm; if it is not already running, in order to trigger or cancel scheduled alarms, or schedule new alarms. The reason for using command line options for this purpose is that if &kalarm; were started without any command line parameters and then sent &DBus; requests, it would start in its default graphical mode, which is clearly undesirable for an inter-program request."
msgstr "As opcións da liña de comandos fornécense para permitir que outros programas inicien o &kalarm; se este non se está xa a executar, para poder así activar ou cancelar alarmas programadas ou programar alarmas novas. A razón para usar opcións da liña de comandos para este propósito é que, se o &kalarm; se iniciase sen parámetros de liña de comandos e despois se lle enviasen peticións de D-Bus, iniciaríase no modo gráfico por omisión, o que claramente non é desexábel para unha petición entre programas."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: index.docbook:4824
